Hey ho.

One of the things that annoys me about wizards is the lack of weapon
choice. Oh sure, there are lots of weapons I *could* use, but once
magicbane is available then anything else seems like pure idiocy. I'd
like to see more meaningful weapon choices for wizards. Also, daggers
just don't feel very 'wizardly' weapons to me, not so much as
quarterstaffs anyway.

How about this:
Give quarterstaffs a small spellcasting bonus (or rather, give any
other wielded weapon a spellcasting hindrance), and then introduce an
artifact staff that has magicbane's curse catching and magic
resistance, and allow wizards to enchant quarterstaffs beyond +5, as
they can with cornuthaums. Then make the first altar gift for wizards
50% magicbane / 50% artifact staff.

This might add a little more variety and interest to wizard games.



